    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1064-a12">

                <pb facs="1156" n="1060" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1060"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 12 in No. 267.]</seg></opener>
                <p rendition="#center">Copies of telegrams sent from the Embassy to the Department
                    of State on February 16, 1898.</p>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sherman</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Secretary, Washington:</hi></p>
                <p>I have received following message from Duke of Connaught:</p>
                <p>“Pray accept my most sincere sympathy at the terriblaaccident which has befallen
                    the warship <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi>. I deeply deplore the loss which
                    your Navy and country have sustained.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">White.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
